cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Gangmu or its rule base in research or a published report, please cite it as below."
title: "Gangmu (纲目): build-time SBOM for embedded C/C++ with a community rule base for chip-vendor SDK components"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The gangmu-sbom authors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/GANGMU-SBOM/gangmu"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.9.0
abstract: >-
  Gangmu identifies open-source components that chip-vendor SDKs have copied,
  renamed and modified in embedded C/C++ firmware, using function-level
  matching against a reproducible community rule base, and produces CycloneDX
  and SPDX SBOMs, VEX, EU Cyber Resilience Act checks and vulnerability report
  drafts.
keywords:
  - SBOM
  - software bill of materials
  - embedded systems
  - firmware
  - C/C++
  - Cyber Resilience Act
  - software composition analysis
  - CycloneDX
  - SPDX
  - VEX
  - vendored code
  - code clone detection
